  PASS: census: the file asserts a start strobe exactly 4 times, one per real block presentation, none of them for the entropy block

----- 4. the entropy is security-relevant, not decorative -----
  PASS: H2 is a masked SHA-512 core, so its entropy input is a side-channel countermeasure
  PASS: hmac_core.sv:145 wires the LFSR output into H2's masking entropy port
  PASS: hmac_core.sv:126 wires the same LFSR output into H1's masking entropy port
  PASS: hmac.sv:311 sources lfsr_seed from the software-writable HMAC512_LFSR_SEED register
  PASS: hmac.sv:159-160 passes that register value straight through to the core

----- 5. scope: the defect is predictability, not a stall -----
  PASS: entropy_digest resets to zero (hmac_core.sv:227), which is what set_entropy then latches
  PASS: the LFSRs are reseeded on every init_cmd (hmac_core.sv:166), so the weak seed is applied per HMAC

